      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 90, a genus-level entry (hybrids, like rose and hosta). Pages: NC State genus page and ASPCA genus page; the cached MBG search had no page. Single care source, so care values are lower confidence; no RHS page read (hardiness left empty, NC State USDA 3 to 9 by species). Pruning groups 1 to 3 differ by type (NC State: type 1 after flowering, type 2 light prune in late winter, type 3 cut nearly to the ground in late winter); not stored. NC State gives 1 to 18 ft long; 550 by 100 cm is the agent's figure for a large climber. Toxicity: NC State high severity (protoanemonin; severe mouth pain and ulcers, dizziness, confusion, convulsions in people; fatalities rare because of the intense bitter taste; contact dermatitis yes) and ASPCA toxic to dogs, cats and horses (salivation, vomiting, diarrhoea). Grade 3 for children and 2 for adults and pets are the agent's mapping; convulsions and confusion have no word in our vocabulary. Watering: moist, well-drained, deep watering; keep_moist a mapping, 4 days a guess. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
